<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Reading Tips | Digital Library & Reading Tracker</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="page">
    <header class="site-header">
      <h1>Reading Tips</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Small habits that make a big difference.</p>
    </header>

    <main class="card">
      <ul class="tips-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Consistency beats intensity.</strong>
          Reading 20 minutes every day adds up faster than one long session a week.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Remove distractions.</strong>
          Put your phone in another room, or use airplane mode during reading time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Set realistic goals.</strong>
          A daily page or time target you'll actually hit beats an ambitious one you'll abandon.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Take notes.</strong>
          Jotting down a sentence per chapter improves retention and gives you something to revisit.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Track your progress.</strong>
          Seeing how far you've come is one of the best motivators to keep going.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </main>

    <nav class="site-nav">
      <a href="/">← Back to Reading Plan</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</body>
</html>